  "name": "Orasho (Kakure Kirishitan hidden-Christian prayer chant)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Orasho are the prayers of the Kakure Kirishitan, the hidden Christians of the Nagasaki islands who kept the faith in secret after Christianity was banned in the early seventeenth century, passing on Latin and Portuguese texts by mouth in forms worn down by centuries of oral transmission. On Ikitsuki Island the men still recite them at their rites, and the sung prayer Gururiyoza was traced by the musicologist Minagawa Tatsuo to O gloriosa Domina, a Latin hymn as sung in sixteenth-century Spain.",
